      {
        "id": 199606,
        "name": "Roger the Alien",
        "username": "Roger_the_Alien",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/r/76d3ee/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2017-06-27T10:51:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Hi John,&nbsp;</p><p>I use an iPad Air 2, the newest version of iOS and Sotm.&nbsp;</p><p>My iPad doesn't use a jailbreak, it wasn't bought used.&nbsp;</p><p>I have almost 35 GB space left and if I use Sotm often no other apps are open in the background, maybe Safari.&nbsp;</p><p>I can't remember that I ever had a crash using Sotm but using this version I have approx. 2 crashes a day.&nbsp;</p><p>It always happens shortly after I open the app, no matter what I do.&nbsp;</p><p>Some minutes ago I opened the app after a crash and I received the achievement for Omnitron-U.&nbsp;</p><p>PS. I assume there is no way to reset it and the screen for unlocking it (again) will never appear, correct?</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>EDIT: I deleted the app and installed it again. Maybe this information matters, Omni-U can't be selected but I still have the achievement.&nbsp;</p>",
